WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.486
While Little John pretended to be a friar, Robin Hood was going to pretend to be a beggar.

2
00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:11.692
But Robin still needed a beggar's clothes.

3
00:00:11.693 --> 00:00:17.627
He walked all morning, enjoying the warm sunshine and fresh smells of springtime.

4
00:00:17.628 --> 00:00:20.502
But he didn't meet any beggars.

5
00:00:20.503 --> 00:00:23.782
"I'm getting hungry," Robin said to himself.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:30.285
He began imagining a delicious meal with eggs, freshly baked bread, a meat pie . . .

7
00:00:30.286 --> 00:00:35.188
Just then Robin rounded a corner and spotted a beggar sitting on a wall.

8
00:00:35.189 --> 00:00:39.202
The man wore a leather cap on top of his curly dark hair.

9
00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:43.567
He was surrounded by all kinds of pouches and bags.

10
00:00:43.568 --> 00:00:46.234
"Hello, fine fellow!" said Robin.

11
00:00:46.235 --> 00:00:49.478
"Do you know where I can find something to eat?"

12
00:00:49.479 --> 00:00:51.887
The beggar had friendly eyes.

13
00:00:51.888 --> 00:00:56.972
"I usually eat just a crust of bread and some water," he said.

14
00:00:56.973 --> 00:01:02.104
Robin laughed. "I can't believe that's all you have in those bags."

15
00:01:02.105 --> 00:01:07.263
"Well, I might have a little cheese," the beggar said slyly.

16
00:01:07.264 --> 00:01:09.517
"Or maybe even some meat.

17
00:01:09.518 --> 00:01:14.488
There's an inn nearby, but they've banned me for stealing a pie.

18
00:01:14.489 --> 00:01:19.158
If you go and buy us drinks, I'll share my food with you."

19
00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:22.513
"Agreed!" said Robin eagerly.

20
00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:26.673
When Robin returned, the two men began eating lunch.

21
00:01:26.674 --> 00:01:29.830
"I'd like to try being a beggar," said Robin.

22
00:01:29.831 --> 00:01:31.724
"Will you sell me your clothes?"

23
00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:35.059
The beggar narrowed his eyes with suspicion.

24
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.650
"You need more than the right clothes to be a good beggar!

25
00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:44.507
It takes a long time to learn how to beg properly.

26
00:01:44.508 --> 00:01:47.864
But let's have a fighting match with our staffs.

27
00:01:47.865 --> 00:01:51.758
If you defeat me, I'll sell you my clothes."

28
00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:58.075
So the two men finished their lunch and picked up their staffs.

29
00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:02.212
In a few minutes the beggar was lying on the ground, rubbing his head.

30
00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:07.259
Robin counted out some coins, and the two men exchanged clothes.

31
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.815
"Thank you, my friend," said Robin.

32
00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:13.722
"Now I'm ready for adventure."

33
00:02:13.723 --> 00:02:18.775
Robin began walking along the road, which led up a gentle hill.

34
00:02:18.776 --> 00:02:24.031
He had walked for a long time when he came across four more beggars, resting in a meadow.

35
00:02:24.032 --> 00:02:26.895
Each man wore a sign around his neck.

36
00:02:26.896 --> 00:02:34.708
As Robin approached, one beggar said, "I hear someone coming!" His sign said, "I'm Deaf."

37
00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:41.216
"He looks like another beggar," said the second man. His sign said, "I'm Blind."

38
00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:48.532
The third man called out to Robin. "Welcome, fellow beggar!" His sign said, "I Can't Talk."

39
00:02:48.533 --> 00:02:52.113
"Come sit with us!" said the fourth man.

40
00:02:52.114 --> 00:02:58.173
He stood up and made room for Robin. His sign said, "I'm Lame."

41
00:02:58.174 --> 00:03:02.543
"Thank you, I will." Robin laughed.

42
00:03:02.544 --> 00:03:05.287
"What a merry group of cheaters!"

43
00:03:05.288 --> 00:03:08.184
"Where did you come from?" asked the blind beggar.

44
00:03:08.185 --> 00:03:12.289
"I spent last night in Sherwood Forest," said Robin.

45
00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.576
"You couldn't pay me to sleep there!" exclaimed the deaf beggar.

46
00:03:16.577 --> 00:03:22.263
"If Robin Hood knew we were tricking people into giving us money, he'd come after us."

47
00:03:22.264 --> 00:03:25.047
"That's right," agreed the lame beggar.

48
00:03:25.048 --> 00:03:28.071
"I wouldn't sleep in Sherwood Forest either.

49
00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:33.822
Not with all the money we're carrying right now for the king. Why, we have—"

50
00:03:33.823 --> 00:03:38.164
"Shh!" The blind beggar silenced the lame man.

51
00:03:38.165 --> 00:03:45.530
"What money are you talking about?" Robin asked pleasantly.

52
00:03:45.531 --> 00:03:49.112
The men grabbed their staffs and leaped to their feet.

53
00:03:49.113 --> 00:03:50.901
They stepped toward Robin.

54
00:03:50.902 --> 00:03:52.730
Robin jumped up too.

55
00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:56.941
"The four of you are going to attack me?" he said.

56
00:03:56.942 --> 00:04:02.211
He twirled his own staff. "Why? I haven't done you any harm."

57
00:04:02.212 --> 00:04:09.505
"Liar! You're a spy!" cried the blind man. "You've heard too much."

58
00:04:09.506 --> 00:04:13.362
He attacked Robin, who quickly knocked him to the ground.

59
00:04:13.363 --> 00:04:17.437
The man rolled over and over on the grass and didn't move.

60
00:04:17.438 --> 00:04:23.565
"Who's next?" Robin rushed at the three men and struck the deaf man.

61
00:04:23.566 --> 00:04:25.886
The deaf man fell to the ground.

62
00:04:25.887 --> 00:04:32.445
The other two beggars looked at Robin with terror, and ran away as fast as they could.

63
00:04:32.446 --> 00:04:34.912
Robin stood there, laughing.

64
00:04:34.913 --> 00:04:38.852
"I've never seen anyone run as fast as that lame man!

65
00:04:38.853 --> 00:04:41.807
Now let's see where that money is."

66
00:04:41.808 --> 00:04:45.076
Robin searched through the beggars' pockets and pouches.

67
00:04:45.077 --> 00:04:49.235
He soon found two hundred pounds in gold coins.

68
00:04:49.236 --> 00:04:53.734
"Those beggars got this money by tricking people," Robin said.

69
00:04:53.735 --> 00:04:56.714
"I'll take it and give it to charity."

70
00:04:56.715 --> 00:05:02.253
Robin started walking along the road, singing and whistling as he went.

71
00:05:02.254 --> 00:05:06.654
Every pretty girl he met smiled and greeted him sweetly.

72
00:05:06.655 --> 00:05:13.031
And every dog he met wagged its tail, and sniffed at his legs, happy to see him.

73
00:05:13.032 --> 00:05:17.297
"Dogs usually mistrust beggars," Robin thought.

74
00:05:17.298 --> 00:05:20.897
"But they always know an honest man by his smell."

75
00:05:20.898 --> 00:05:26.660
Robin was an honest man—in his own way.

